							<div class="smalltext">
								Jr. Member<br />
								<img src="http://masslinemedia.com/smf/Themes/safgrey105/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://masslinemedia.com/smf/Themes/safgrey105/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><br />
								Posts: 69<br />
								<br />
								<div style="overflow: auto; width: 100%;"><img src="http://www.filmguideseattle.com/images/backfocuschart.jpg" width="65" height="65" alt="" border="0" /></div><br />
								
								
								<a href="aim:goim?screenname=TikiLittle&amp;message=Hi.+Are+you+there?"><img src="http://masslinemedia.com/smf/Themes/safgrey105/images/aim.gif" alt="TikiLittle" border="0" /></a>
								<br />
								<a href="http://masslinemedia.com/smf/index.php?action=profile;u=717"><img src="http://masslinemedia.com/smf/Themes/safgrey105/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
								<a href="mailto:tiki_little@hotmail.com"><img src="http://masslinemedia.com/smf/Themes/safgrey105/images/email_sm.gif" alt="Email" title="Email" border="0" /></a>
							</div>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://masslinemedia.com/smf/index.php?topic=2209.msg27413#msg27413"><img src="http://masslinemedia.com/smf/Themes/safgrey105/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://masslinemedia.com/smf/index.php?topic=2209.msg27413#msg27413">Re: (Rich) White People and Blue Scholars</a></b>
									<div class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #2 on:</b> May 16, 2007, 10:38:01 am &#187;</div></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							<div style="overflow: auto; width: 100%;">Yes, I agree that having a critical engagement is very important. I think the Blue Scholars need to release their lyrics to their website because I have heard many people complain that they want to follow the lyrics, but they can&#039;t.<br /><br />I disagree with the statement about &quot;rich white men&quot; are buying this album. I&#039;ve followed the Blue Scholars to many shows in the last year and a half. I&#039;ve been to different university campuses, high school auditoriums, and venues. Each time I&#039;ve seen a wide variety of people. So, I argue that rich can&#039;t be applied to Blue Scholars fans.<br /><br />I agree that predominatly their is a white listening base in Seattle, but as a white adult, I think that is hard to seperate as you said from being in Seattle. When I peruse home-made videos, I see a lot of energy being put into the South Side, which is great. <br /><br />The other part that your argument doesn&#039;t touch upon is that Hip hop is largely a youth-oriented movement.</div>
						</td>
					</tr>
