						<td valign="top" width="16%" rowspan="2" style="overflow: hidden;">
							<b><a href="http://masslinemedia.com/smf/index.php?action=profile;u=63" title="View the profile of Meiotch">Meiotch</a></b>
							<div class="smalltext">
								Full Member<br />
								<img src="http://masslinemedia.com/smf/Themes/safgrey105/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://masslinemedia.com/smf/Themes/safgrey105/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://masslinemedia.com/smf/Themes/safgrey105/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><br />
								Posts: 241<br />
								<br />
								<div style="overflow: auto; width: 100%;"><img src="http://cbimg9.com/graphics/07/07/06/32979c.jpg" width="65" height="65" alt="" border="0" /></div><br />
								its a test, im a mess right?<br />
								<br />
								
								
								
								<br />
								<a href="http://masslinemedia.com/smf/index.php?action=profile;u=63"><img src="http://masslinemedia.com/smf/Themes/safgrey105/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
							</div>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://masslinemedia.com/smf/index.php?topic=2209.msg27437#msg27437"><img src="http://masslinemedia.com/smf/Themes/safgrey105/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://masslinemedia.com/smf/index.php?topic=2209.msg27437#msg27437">Re: (Rich) White People and Blue Scholars</a></b>
									<div class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #13 on:</b> May 16, 2007, 12:28:46 pm &#187;</div></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							<div style="overflow: auto; width: 100%;">Just because a fan doesnt come to a show and spend $30-40 on merch and cd&#039;s, doesnt mean that fan is not engaged in active listening and progression of the message in the Scholar&#039;s lyrics.  I myself am white, but that in no way represents my ability to internalize the struggle of those around me, especially those in a position of poverty.<br /><br /> &quot;Yet, I still can&#039;t help but get frustrated when I see a crowd of middle and upper-class white folks singing about destroying the systems of privilege which they have gained so much from. I&#039;m not saying that people shouldn&#039;t feel free to listen and enjoy the music they like.&quot;  - How do you know that these kids are middle to upper-class? Expensive shoes? Clothes?  check the end of &quot;Still Got Love&quot;....because you see what someone represents on the outside, you know them enough to judge them on the inside?  Claiming someone else&#039;s struggle as your own is definetly not the thing to do, but recognizing others struggles and even doing minor things to change your view and your friends views of them is a small victory in itself.  I know simply saying &quot;hello&quot; or &quot;have a nice day&quot; to someone or giving a homeless person money isnt as strong as statement as marching in an Immigration rights rally, but its progress nonetheless.  I have become very aware of the mistreatment of Fillipinos (in the homeland) as well as the mistreatment of others in America, and now can bring that to the table when talking with people of any class or race, which further advances the message.  Admittedly, Im sure theres whites who listen to the Scholars just because, but if they are at your shows, singing your lyrics, what is wrong with that?  The best place to invoke change is with those who you feel is holding you down (but I have a feeling its not those 20 something&#039;s at concerts)</div>
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext" width="85%">
